Draft:
Nixle Sparkwrench crept through Stranglethorn's humidity, his boots squelching in the mud. Beside him, nothing stirred—at least, nothing visible. "Quiet, Selara," he whispered to the air. A giggle answered, sultry and close. 

They approached the Bloodsail Buccaneers. Nixle pointed at a sleeping scout. "Seduce." The air shimmered; the scout stood, entranced, as Nixle's Shadow Bolt flew true. When the pirate's companions charged, they saw only the tiny Gnome. 

"Where's the other one?" a troll snarled. 

Nixle smiled as Lash of Pain struck from nowhere. "She's shy." 

The Voidwalker back in Ironforge could keep his health bar safe; here, among the dense foliage and wandering Horde, being unseen was survival. The Succubus's kiss—Soothing Kiss—kept her threat low, her invisibility kept her hidden, and Nixle loved that his enemies never saw the blade coming until it was buried in their backs.

